## TestMu AI MCP Server

- [TestMu AI MCP Server](https://www.testmuai.com/mcp/): Connect AI agents and IDEs directly to your test data through a unified MCP server, no manual transfers. Works with Claude, Cursor, GitHub Copilot, OpenAI Codex CLI, and other MCP clients.

The TestMu AI MCP Server is a remote Model Context Protocol (MCP) server that connects AI clients and IDEs directly to your TestMu AI testing environment, so you can orchestrate tests, debug failures, and analyze results through natural language without leaving your editor. Server URL: https://mcp.lambdatest.com/mcp (OAuth authentication; Streamable HTTP or STDIO transport). Universal setup: add the server URL to your client config, or run `npx mcp-remote@latest https://mcp.lambdatest.com/mcp`.

Supported AI clients: Claude Code, Claude Desktop, claude.ai (Web), Cursor, GitHub Copilot (VS Code), OpenAI Codex CLI, Cline (VS Code), Continue, Antigravity, and any MCP-compatible client that supports Streamable HTTP or STDIO transports.

- [MCP Server for HyperExecute](https://www.testmuai.com/hyperexecute-mcp-server/): HyperExecute MCP Server understands your code, auto-generates test commands, builds configs, and fetches docs using tools tailored for each task.
- [Browser Automation MCP Alternative](https://www.testmuai.com/browser-automation-mcp/): An agent-native layer above browser automation MCP. Kane CLI takes plain-English objectives and returns a verified pass or fail, not raw MCP primitives.
- [MCP Server Setup Docs](https://www.testmuai.com/support/docs/testmu-mcp-server.md): Step-by-step configuration for Claude, Cursor, GitHub Copilot, OpenAI Codex CLI, Cline, Continue, and other MCP clients.

The server exposes five tool groups. HyperExecute: AI-native test orchestration that auto-generates test runner commands and HyperExecute YAML, monitors jobs, and surfaces session details. Automation: triage and debug automation test failures by pulling execution data plus command, network, and console logs to identify root cause inside your IDE. SmartUI: debug visual regressions with natural-language summaries of pixel, layout, DOM, and perceptual differences from any SmartUI comparison run. Accessibility: run accessibility checks on hosted URLs or local React apps and get detailed remediation guidance. Test Manager: create and manage projects, folders, test cases, test runs, and milestones, and record results.

